'Piña Colada':['rum','tropical','50 ml white or aged rum; 30 ml cream of coconut; 90 ml pineapple juice','Shake or blend with crushed ice; garnish pineapple.','Creamy, tropical, sweet-tart, coconut-rich.','Officially linked with Puerto Rico and San Juan, with competing mid-20th-century origin stories. It became Puerto Rico’s official drink in 1978.'],
'Caipirinha':['cachaça','sour','60 ml cachaça; 1 lime; 2 tsp fine sugar','Muddle lime wedges gently with sugar; add cachaça and ice; stir.','Fresh lime oils, grassy cane, direct sweetness.','Brazil’s national cocktail, made with cachaça. Its exact origin is uncertain; early medicinal lime-and-spirit preparations are sometimes cited.'],
